/TERMINAL EMULATOR FOR USE ON A PDP8/12   PAL8-V12B 25-AUG-87 PAGE 2

             /INITIALIZATION CODE FOR TERMIN PROGRAM                 -JVZ-

             /THIS CODE SCANS THE COMMAND LINE WHICH CALLS THE TERMIN PRO-
             /GRAM, LOOKING FOR THE FOLLOWING CONFIGURATION OPTIONS:

             /       /NORMAL[=XX]    -       USE 'KL8E' BREAK; TLS=6XX6
             /       /DECSTA[=2,3]   -       BAUD-RATE BREAK; SLU2,SLU3
             /       /SPECIAL        -       SPECIAL BREAK; DVC=40,41
             /       /SPEED=NNNN     -       SET BAUD RATE (50-19200)
             /       /BAUDRATE=NNNN  -       SAME AS /SPEED=NNNN
             /       /INPUT=XX       -       CHANGE INPUT DEVICE CODE
             /       /OUTPUT=XX      -       CHANGE OUTPUT DEVICE CODE
             /       /ARROW          -       SHOW CTRL CHARS AS '^,CHAR'
             /       /VERSION        -       PRINT VERSION NUMBER
             /       /HELP           -       PRINT OPTION SUMMARY
             /       /PERMANENT      -       MODIFY PROGRAM LOAD FILE

             /OPTIONS MAY BE SPECIFIED IN ANY ORDER; NO SPACES ARE PERMIT-
             /TED BETWEEN THE '/' AND THE OPTION WORD, NOR BETWEEN THE '='
             /SIGN AND THE NUMERIC PARAMETER.  SINGLE-LETTER ABBREVIATIONS
             /MAY BE USED, HOWEVER, SINCE ONLY THE FIRST LETTER IS TESTED:

             /EXAMPLE 1:             .R TERMIN /N=46 /PERM

             /THIS SPECIFIES A 'NORMAL' INTERFACE (KL8E, KL8JA, M707, ETC.)
             /SET FOR DEVICE CODES 46 (INPUT) AND 47 (OUTPUT).  THE CHANGES
             /WILL BE SAVED IN SYS:TERMIN.SV.  BOTH /NORMAL AND /DECSTATION
             /REMOVE CONTROL CHARACTER FLAGGING UNLESS /ARROW IS SPECIFIED.

             /EXAMPLE 2:             .TER/D/S=300/P

             /THIS RUNS THE PROGRAM USING THE OS/78 CCL COMMAND, SPECIFYING
             /THE '/DECSTATION', '300 BAUD' AND '/PERMANENT' OPTIONS.  THE
             /OPTIONS CAN THEN BE OMITTED IN SUBSEQUENT CALLS UNTIL, (SAY),
             /IT IS NECESSARY TO SPECIFY A DIFFERENT BAUD RATE OR SWITCH TO
             /A DIFFERENT PORT.  ('SLU3' IS THE DEFAULT: '/D=2' SWITCHES TO
             /'SLU2'.  'DECMATE' (VT/278) PROCESSORS CAN ONLY USE 'SLU3'.)

             /THE FOLLOWING ERROR MESSAGES MAY BE PRINTED ON THE TERMINAL,
             /FOLLOWED BY A RETURN TO THE OS/8 MONITOR:

             /       NOT UNDER BATCH!               (CAN'T RUN UNDER BATCH)
             /       INPUT DVC = OUTPUT DVC         (CODES MUST BE UNIQUE!)
             /       BAD SPEED OR BAUD RATE         (SEE NOTE BELOW)
             /       WRITE ERROR ON LOAD DEV        (UPDATE (/PERM) FAILED)

             /THE FOLLOWING ARE THE ONLY BAUD RATES AVAILABLE (VT/78,'278):
             /50,75,110,134,150,300,600,1200,1800,2000,2400,3600,4800,7200,
             /9600 AND 19200; THE DEFAULT FOR THE /D OPTION IS 9600.  (THIS
             /CAN BE CHANGED BY PATCHING LOCATION '200' OF THE '.SV' FILE.)

